WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.736
-Welcome back to "Late Night,"
everybody.

00:00:02.736 --> 00:00:04.003
Here with the cast of "Nope."
It is so great to have you guys.

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:07.607
So, Jupiter's Claim
is the fictional theme park

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:08.641
in this film...
-Whoo!

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:10.209
-...that is now being
re-created.

00:00:10.209 --> 00:00:12.745
They've actually rebuilt it
at Universal Studios,

00:00:12.745 --> 00:00:15.147
open to the public tomorrow.
-So, yes, this --

00:00:15.147 --> 00:00:17.083
I'm very proud of this.
Look, listen to this.

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:19.752
This is the first time
that a back --

00:00:19.752 --> 00:00:23.990
Universal Studios California
backlot tour has had the --

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:27.760
the set at the same time
as the movie's being released.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:30.430
It just goes to show you how
much they believe in this film.

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:32.732
And it is. It's the --
It's the theme park

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:36.770
that Steven Yeun's character
owns in the film.

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:42.341
And let's just say it's --
it's the -- the site of some --

00:00:42.341 --> 00:00:45.144
some uncanny weirdness...
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.144 --> 00:00:48.081
...and also, some --
some horrible, horrible things.

00:00:48.081 --> 00:00:49.548
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.548 --> 00:00:52.118
But it's cheery, and it's happy.
-Makes me very happy.

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:53.619
Jordan, we've talked in the past
when you were on.

00:00:53.619 --> 00:00:55.054
We've known each other
for over 20 years.

00:00:55.054 --> 00:00:56.723
We've gone to some amusement
parks together over the years.

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:59.592
-We have. Well, it's very --
it is very funny.

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:02.128
We're here pretending like
we haven't been, like,

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:04.196
inebriated on 20 different
substances...

00:01:04.196 --> 00:01:05.331
-Yeah, exactly.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:07.200
-...in a Dutch theme park...
-Yeah.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.903
-...like, sweating over
the bust of, like, a --

00:01:10.903 --> 00:01:12.905
of a fantasy Dutch guy.
-Yeah, we've had --

00:01:12.905 --> 00:01:14.307
We should probably leave it
at that, but we had some...

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:16.676
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:18.778
We had some -- yeah.
-I wanted more.

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:20.280
-Yeah.
-It was all legal substances.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:22.949
-I'm sorry
to play Daniel's mom here,

00:01:22.949 --> 00:01:26.085
but I think there's some things
we're not supposed to talk about

00:01:26.085 --> 00:01:27.720
on television.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.489
-So good, man.
So good.

00:01:29.489 --> 00:01:31.824
-Now, do you -- are you someone
who likes theme parks?

00:01:31.824 --> 00:01:33.359
-Oh, my gosh.
I love theme parks.

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:35.061
And I was so excited.
Like he's saying,

00:01:35.061 --> 00:01:36.662
this is the first time
it's ever happened before,

00:01:36.662 --> 00:01:38.598
so I was like -- I remember,
I kept asking Jordan,

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:40.233
I said, "Is it gonna leave?"

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:41.300
He's like,
"Nope, it's here to stay."

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.736
I'm like, "It's forever?"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:46.239
We start playing games.
I got to do --

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:47.806
I mean, I had my Jupe jingle.

00:01:47.806 --> 00:01:49.709
You rocking a little bit
of the merch, Lil Key --

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:51.477
You know what I mean?
You want to show them?

00:01:51.477 --> 00:01:53.646
-Oh, this -- This is just
a reference to one of

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:56.749
my favorite movies from
the '90s, "Kid Sheriff."

00:01:56.749 --> 00:01:57.917
-Which one?
-"Kid Sheriff."

00:01:57.917 --> 00:01:59.151
-Oh, "kid Sheriff."
There you go.

00:01:59.151 --> 00:02:00.586
Yeah, great -- a great film.
-Yeah, which is --

00:02:00.586 --> 00:02:02.755
which, of course, Jupe's Claim
is loosely based off of.

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:05.191
-Yeah, yeah. there you go.
You got to take your dad,

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:07.927
Brandon, to this part of the
park before it opened, right?

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:09.462
-Yeah.
It's -- It's insane,

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:11.330
because my dad
came to California.

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:13.833
I've lived there for 11 years,
and he's never been able

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:16.336
to make it out until now
for the premiere of the film.

00:02:16.336 --> 00:02:17.770
And he was like,
"Oh, I've always wanted to go

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.271
to Universal.
I'm gonna buy a ticket."

00:02:19.271 --> 00:02:21.607
I was like, "No, no! I just
did a movie with them, man!"

00:02:21.607 --> 00:02:24.210
And I was able to get us, like,
the V.I.P. tour,

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:26.713
and it was incredible and, like,
this is crazy to me.

00:02:26.713 --> 00:02:29.682
Like, my life is insane.
V.I.P. tour of Universal.

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:32.218
Jordan Peele is next to me.
Keke Palmer, Daniel Kaluuya.

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:34.520
I'm on "Late Night
with Seth Meyers."

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.856
Like, bruh...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:39.192
God bless, man.
This is insane to me, man.

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:41.527
I'm like -- just like,
"What is going on?"

00:02:41.527 --> 00:02:44.797
-The previous younger kid
to go pro, that was his peak.

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:46.199
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:48.067
-You just raced by him.

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:50.069
That's, like, a footnote
on your bio now.

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:52.305
-Cheers man, cheers.
-You --

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:54.240
Do you also -- What about you?

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.441
Roller coasters?
You like any of that?

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:56.676
-Eh.
-Okay.

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:58.677
-Stress.
-What about haunted houses?

00:02:58.677 --> 00:03:00.213
-Oh, yeah, no.
I don't like those.

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:01.547
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.547 --> 00:03:03.115
But we -- but me and my boys,
we got kicked out of one.

00:03:03.115 --> 00:03:04.584
We got kicked out of one.

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:07.486
-How old were you when you got
kicked out of a haunted house?

00:03:07.486 --> 00:03:08.488
-26.

00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:10.690
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.292
-Well, that's their fault
for letting you in.

00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:13.992
-The actors --
The actors were starting --

00:03:13.992 --> 00:03:15.494
they tried touching us.
-Man, no.

00:03:15.494 --> 00:03:16.696
-Okay.
-So one of -- one of them

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:18.798
threw a punch, and then,
they said we're banned.

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:20.265
-Wait. So one of your friends
threw a punch?

00:03:20.265 --> 00:03:22.302
-Yeah, one of my friends did.
Finally were like, "Aah!"

00:03:22.302 --> 00:03:24.837
They were like --
and they were like, "Leave."

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:27.006
And the actors --
the actors broke character.

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:28.208
And I was like,
"What are you doing?

00:03:28.208 --> 00:03:29.541
You're supposed to commit."
Like --

00:03:29.541 --> 00:03:30.876
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:03:30.876 --> 00:03:33.045
In real life,
when you punch a mummy,

00:03:33.045 --> 00:03:35.247
they're not like, "Get out!"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.247 --> 00:03:38.517
-Anybody -- Anybody anywhere
that jumps out and surprises you

00:03:38.517 --> 00:03:41.921
has to be ready to be caught
with a punch at any moment.

00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:44.924
It's just a risk you're taking.
-I don't -- you know what?

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:49.295
I'm sorry to jump in defense
of the haunted-house staff,

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:50.796
but I think they might assume

00:03:50.796 --> 00:03:52.231
that you know
that's gonna happen.

00:03:52.231 --> 00:03:53.933
-You're right.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:56.402
You're right.
-But we believe --

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:57.904
We're believing
in their depiction.

00:03:57.904 --> 00:03:59.272
-Are you saying
that you were doing

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:00.873
a performance as good as theirs?

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:04.377
-Yes! I'm matching the energy
that they're giving me.

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:06.078
I'm like, "Oh, ay!"
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:06.078 --> 00:04:08.081
-It's immersive.
He's truly immersive.

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:09.982
-Very, very meta.
-Yeah.

00:04:09.982 --> 00:04:12.585
Well, I remember we --
we went once had dinner here

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:14.120
at one of those theme
restaurants, you know,

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:15.187
the sort of, like,
horror-themed.

00:04:15.187 --> 00:04:17.723
-Yes.
-And I have great respect

00:04:17.723 --> 00:04:21.027
for people who -- who in those
situations really sell it,

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:22.561
like, actors who is put
their all into it.

00:04:22.561 --> 00:04:24.396
-Yes, we were at
the "Jekyll and Hyde."

00:04:24.396 --> 00:04:26.632
-Yeah.
-And this was at a period

00:04:26.632 --> 00:04:28.501
15 years ago,
where I was writing

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:29.902
my first script
for you to star in.

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:33.506
-Yeah. And I'm sorry
I turned you down.

00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:35.742
-You said no?
-I didn't say no.

00:04:35.742 --> 00:04:37.443
-It was not that.
-Yeah.

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:39.145
-I didn't finish the script,
and you were very successful.

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:41.047
-What was it about?
-He told me it was either

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:44.417
me or you for "Get Out."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:45.417
Originally,
it was called "Get In."

00:04:45.417 --> 00:04:48.888
-He said,
"If Kaluuya says no..."

00:04:48.888 --> 00:04:50.323
I think -- I don't think it
would have worked with me.

00:04:50.323 --> 00:04:52.124
-Do you -- would you...
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.124 --> 00:04:54.627
...would you be...

00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:59.198
Yeah, I mean, I would definitely
consider a sequel to "Get Out."

00:04:59.198 --> 00:05:00.566
-Yeah.
-If you would consider.

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:02.167
-It is -- but it is very funny.

00:05:02.167 --> 00:05:04.837
Again, I was -- I was saying
this to your cast backstage.

00:05:04.837 --> 00:05:07.339
But we -- you know, to echo
what I said earlier, you know,

00:05:07.339 --> 00:05:09.475
a lot of the things we did,
we were improvising together

00:05:09.475 --> 00:05:11.577
in Amsterdam, we used to go to
horror movies all the time.

00:05:11.577 --> 00:05:13.046
-Yes.
-A large group of us.

00:05:13.046 --> 00:05:15.648
And now, you know, we can't
believe that one of the things

00:05:15.648 --> 00:05:18.418
we all get to do together now
is go see Jordan's new movie.

00:05:18.418 --> 00:05:21.521
It is -- It is an incredible
thing to take.

00:05:21.521 --> 00:05:24.790
And you have a great eye
for talent, my friend.

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:25.958
-Can I ask a question?
-Yeah.

00:05:25.958 --> 00:05:28.428
-Did you know --
Did you know that he was gonna

00:05:28.428 --> 00:05:30.296
direct horrors and be into that?

00:05:30.296 --> 00:05:32.698
-I knew he would be
incredibly successful,

00:05:32.698 --> 00:05:34.133
but I would have predicted
"Key &amp; Peele"

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:35.601
before I would've
predicted this. Right?

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:37.236
When "Key &amp; Peele" happened,
I was like, "Of course."

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:39.305
-Yeah, yeah.
-But, yeah, I mean, this --

00:05:39.305 --> 00:05:41.874
I think no one could have
predicted this.

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:43.209
-Jordan, I just live
for you, man.

00:05:43.209 --> 00:05:45.544
-Like, I -- well, hey.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:45.544 --> 00:05:48.181
And I'm --
-You're the best, dude.

00:05:48.181 --> 00:05:50.216
-This is it.

00:05:50.216 --> 00:05:52.084
It all worked out.
-It's called "Nope."

00:05:52.084 --> 00:05:54.086
It's called "Nope."
-It's called "Nope."

00:05:54.086 --> 00:05:55.120
It's in theaters.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:56.655
Oh, and this is really exciting,
you guys.

00:05:56.655 --> 00:05:59.692
"Nope" opens in theaters
and IMAX tomorrow,

00:05:59.692 --> 00:06:01.727
and courtesy of our friends
at IMAX --

00:06:01.727 --> 00:06:04.597
I've got a card right here --
everyone here in the audience

00:06:04.597 --> 00:06:07.700
is getting two tickets
to see "Nope" in IMAX.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:08.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:10.936
How about that?
They're all in it.

00:06:10.936 --> 00:06:12.371
He directed it.

00:06:12.371 --> 00:06:14.940
Don't miss it.
It's great.

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:16.909
We'll be right back.
Even if you're an alien,

00:06:16.909 --> 00:06:19.212
we'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

